  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_006 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) at 0.6530 accuracy. Image alone (resnet50) is very weak at 0.2079, and scgpt underperforms scvi_n200 in multiprofile settings. The critical open question is whether adding the image modality to the strongest RNA pipeline can improve upon 0.6530, or whether the weak image signal will only add noise. This experiment (config_032) directly extends the best-performing RNA configuration by adding resnet50 image features with concat fusion, keeping all other settings (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer) identical. It isolates the effect of multimodal fusion on the proven-best RNA setup. With 3 experiments remaining after this, confirming or ruling out the multimodal direction early is essential: if it helps, I can refine fusion strategy (weighted) or image encoder (ViT) in the last 3 slots; if it hurts, I can focus remaining budget on RNA-only refinements or alternative image encoders."
}

